1
00:00:00,370 --> 00:00:01,580
Why
is ‘The furniture

2
00:00:01,620 --> 00:00:03,792
are expensive’
wrong?

3
00:00:05,137 --> 00:00:06,390
Look at what
furniture

4
00:00:06,430 --> 00:00:08,635
contains:
a chair, a table,

5
00:00:08,675 --> 00:00:10,130
a sofa, a bed.

6
00:00:10,170 --> 00:00:11,799
Many different
things.

7
00:00:12,237 --> 00:00:14,320
But English doesn’t
name each one.

8
00:00:14,360 --> 00:00:15,784
It groups
them together

9
00:00:15,824 --> 00:00:17,811
and names them
as one unit:

10
00:00:17,851 --> 00:00:19,043
furniture.

11
00:00:19,470 --> 00:00:20,958
Why? Because
furniture

12
00:00:20,998 --> 00:00:22,910
is not the name
of an object.

13
00:00:22,950 --> 00:00:25,170
It’s the name
of the whole collection.

14
00:00:25,210 --> 00:00:27,051
The word comes
from ‘furnish’:

15
00:00:27,091 --> 00:00:29,300
everything you
furnish a room with.

16
00:00:29,837 --> 00:00:31,414
And a unit
means one.

17
00:00:31,454 --> 00:00:32,998
One is always
singular.

18
00:00:33,038 --> 00:00:34,647
We can’t add
s to one.

19
00:00:34,687 --> 00:00:35,303
So:

20
00:00:35,343 --> 00:00:37,459
‘The furniture
is expensive.’

21
00:00:38,403 --> 00:00:39,718
The same logic
works for

22
00:00:39,758 --> 00:00:41,072
the whole family.

23
00:00:41,112 --> 00:00:43,577
Luggage:
bags and suitcases.

24
00:00:43,617 --> 00:00:45,872
Equipment:
tools and machines.

25
00:00:45,912 --> 00:00:47,999
Clothing:
shirts and trousers.

26
00:00:48,039 --> 00:00:49,941
Crockery:
plates and cups.

27
00:00:49,981 --> 00:00:52,409
Stationery:
pens and paper.

28
00:00:52,937 --> 00:00:54,403
Notice
the endings:

29
00:00:54,443 --> 00:00:55,821
luggage,
equipment,

30
00:00:55,861 --> 00:00:57,490
clothing,
crockery.

31
00:00:57,530 --> 00:00:58,702
These endings
often build

32
00:00:58,742 --> 00:01:00,991
a word for a whole
collection.

33
00:01:01,537 --> 00:01:03,194
So each one
is one unit,

34
00:01:03,234 --> 00:01:04,852
with a singular
verb:

35
00:01:04,892 --> 00:01:06,114
the luggage
is heavy,

36
00:01:06,154 --> 00:01:07,579
the equipment
is new,

37
00:01:07,619 --> 00:01:09,231
my clothing
is wet.

38
00:01:09,770 --> 00:01:11,083
Need to count
them?

39
00:01:11,123 --> 00:01:12,309
Count a piece:

40
00:01:12,349 --> 00:01:13,859
two pieces
of furniture,

41
00:01:13,899 --> 00:01:15,410
three pieces
of luggage,

42
00:01:15,450 --> 00:01:17,152
an item
of clothing.

43
00:01:17,703 --> 00:01:19,609
So don’t memorise
the list.

44
00:01:19,649 --> 00:01:20,759
See the unit:

45
00:01:20,799 --> 00:01:22,162
many things,
one name,

46
00:01:22,202 --> 00:01:23,501
one verb.

